From 60aa3693762d699fba5b408b64c4dde5a77c00ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 12:57:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 367/369] rtrafd: merge MAC-unknown IP-keyed flows into the
 real device slot; trim Roaming Assistant help

cli_slot(): a flow whose source MAC can't be resolved (offline device, aged-out
ARP/bridge entry) fell back to keying the client by its IP - creating a SECOND
slot for a device already tracked by MAC. The same device then appeared twice
(once by MAC, once with the IP jammed into the "mac" field) in health.json, the
Prometheus/analytics export, and the Traffic Analyzer. Now, before creating an
IP-keyed slot, reuse any existing MAC-keyed slot with the same IP. IPv4-looking
keys only; the "router" bucket and real MACs are untouched. Runs only on a cache
miss on the uncommon MAC-unknown path, so no hot-path cost for known clients.

Also: the Roaming Assistant help on Reaper_WiFiPro.asp (RWFP_14) is trimmed to
just "0 = off" (was "0 = off; otherwise the dBm threshold to disconnect weak
clients") per owner.

v2.3.0.
